@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0

# ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the game's anti-aliasing. Its only live AA pass is SMAA, run as the
// three FilterSMAAEdge / FilterSMAAWeight / FilterSMAABlend passes at the very
// end of the frame. The binary also loads MLAA (FilterShaderEdgeMLAA / MLAA /
// BlendMLAA), DLAA (FilterShaderDLAA1 / DLAA2) and FilterSMAACopy programs, but
// nothing draws with them, and there is no FXAA filter.
//
// One flag decides whether the SMAA chain runs. It is the AND of three
// conditions: the AA quality setting allows it, the game is docked, and the
// renderer's SMAA feature bit is set. When it is true the tone-mapped image is
// redirected into a scratch target and the SMAA chain blends it onto the real
// one; when it is false the image goes straight to the real target and the
// chain is skipped. Handheld mode already takes that second path every frame,
// so forcing the flag to zero produces the engine's own no-AA output rather
// than a new code path.
//
// This patches the frame code, not a config default, so an option screen or a
// settings file cannot turn it back on.

@enabled
00402AE0 19008052   // MOVZ W25,#0 (was AND W25,W9,W8,LSR#26 = the SMAA enable flag)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_036, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
